{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["The line panel 'Posterior vs prior' is malformed when both likelihoods are zero (e.g. likeA=0, likeNotA=0): every point is filtered out, leaving an empty series/points array, which the renderer rejects. The panel must degrade gracefully (e.g. emit an unavailable panel or a series with a defined fallback) instead of an empty points array.", "The odds panel reports likelihoodRatio as undefined when pEnA=0 even if pEA>0, but the excerpt's odds statement requires the ratio to be defined; more importantly the panel's 'Product' and 'Posterior odds' rows can silently disagree with the displayed posterior when pEnA=0 and pEA>0 (posterior odds is finite/infinite while product is 'undefined'). The odds table should consistently mark all four rows undefined whenever the ratio is undefined, so the illustrative check never contradicts the posterior metrics.", "The line panel filters out null points, so at the boundary where the denominator vanishes for some priors (e.g. likeA=0, likeNotA>0 gives d=0 only at p=0) the curve silently drops that prior value rather than showing the undefined boundary; the exploration 'Impossible evidence boundary' therefore cannot render. The panel should represent the undefined region explicitly (e.g. keep the point with null y and mark unavailable) rather than removing points."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "Uninformative evidence leaves prior unchanged", "state": {"priorA": 0.3, "likeA": 0.5, "likeNotA": 0.5}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0.3, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 0.7, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Known analytic posterior", "state": {"priorA": 0.3, "likeA": 0.9, "likeNotA": 0.2}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "formula": "(0.9 * 0.3) / (0.9 * 0.3 + 0.2 * (1 - 0.3))", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "formula": "0.9 * 0.3 + 0.2 * (1 - 0.3)", "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Zero denominator is undefined", "state": {"priorA": 0.4, "likeA": 0, "likeNotA": 0}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": null}, {"path": "metrics.0.defined", "value": false}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Prior at boundary with positive likelihood", "state": {"priorA": 0, "likeA": 0.9, "likeNotA": 0.2}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 1, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Odds product equals posterior odds", "state": {"priorA": 0.3, "likeA": 0.9, "likeNotA": 0.2}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "formula": "(0.3 / 0.7) * (0.9 / 0.2) / (1 + (0.3 / 0.7) * (0.9 / 0.2))", "atol": 1e-08}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Posterior masses sum to one when defined", "expression": "!o.metrics[0].defined || Math.abs(o.metrics[0].value + o.metrics[1].value - 1) < 1e-9"}, {"name": "Marginal equals sum of joint masses", "expression": "Math.abs(o.metrics[2].value - (o.metrics[3].value + o.metrics[4].value)) < 1e-12"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 46.773}
